# Cross-machine handoff

At the start of a session (especially on a different PC/Mac than the last
known work), read `docs/CURSOR_HANDOFF.md` before making large changes.

- It lists what is already shipped, live config, and the priority backlog.
- The user may assign a **different** task than the backlog — still use the
  handoff so you do not redo finished work or invent a new Firebase/repo.
- After meaningful work, update the **Session log** in that file, plus
  `docs/CURSOR_CHANGES_FOR_CLAUDE.md`, then commit/push with an overall note.
